    {
      "id": 326,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -5080,
        90
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        380
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "title": "Multi-view frames to one .vox",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Multi-view frames to one .vox\n1. Zip every view of every frame as `<anything>-<view>-<number>.png`, or put them in `front/`, `left/`, `back/` and `right/` folders: `girl-run-front-01.png`, `left/girl-run-01.png`... Use 2 to 4 views, the same ones in every frame, with the background in alpha and the same pixel scale in every picture.\n2. Press **Upload zip** on Load Numbered Views and press **Run** once; with **whole_zip** each frame queues the next. Keep this window open meanwhile.\n\nThe loader frames every view the way Pixal3D's rig expects: one square side for every view and frame, the widest extent of the whole animation filling 1/1.1 of it, every view at the same height and each centered on where the subject moves in it. Views not in the zip are left out.\n\nBoth save nodes use **placement: grid**, so every frame is the same size and keeps its place in the grid: the frames line up as an animation.\n\nEach frame is saved as `output/vox/characters-views/<number>.vox`, and every run rewrites `output/vox/characters-views.vox` with all of them, sharing one palette."
      ]
    }
  ],
